From d2546cec226a6925beb93edafce3ce4ebdfe191f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rnsbox <rnsbox@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:27:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] buildroot: ship an explicit /etc/securetty
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The vendor-turned-rnsbox rootfs carried an EMPTY /etc/securetty. busybox
is_tty_secure() semantics: a missing or empty file means every tty is
secure, while any file with a non-matching line means that tty is not —
so root console login worked everywhere, but by accident, and the file
was one stray line away from locking root out of every console.

Ship the explicit list of consoles rnsbox drives (console, ttyS0-3,
ttyAMA0/1, hvc0): the serial rescue path stays documented-and-
intentional, unknown ttys no longer implicitly accept root, and the
emulated console (qemu -M virt, ttyAMA0) is covered. root keeps its
password; the file only matters for actual console logins.
---
 buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/securetty | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/securetty

diff --git a/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/securetty b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/securetty
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..9e1311c7f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/buildroot/board/cvitek/SG200X/overlay/etc/securetty
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# RNSBox: the vendor-turned-rnsbox rootfs shipped an EMPTY /etc/securetty,
+# which makes busybox login refuse root on every tty (no password prompt —
+# just "Login incorrect"). That broke the serial-console rescue path the
+# README documents and any emulated console (qemu's ttyAMA0). List the
+# consoles rnsbox actually drives; root still needs its password.
+console
+ttyS0
+ttyS1
+ttyS2
+ttyS3
+ttyAMA0
+ttyAMA1
+hvc0
-- 
